==============================================================================
THREAD C (1): CJJ linear-vs-nonlinear obstruction -- PRECISE + VERIFIED
==============================================================================

--- (L1) linear-combination closure (CJJ view (c)) ---
A code is LINEAR iff its codeword set is closed under F_p-linear combination
(= an additive subgroup). CJJ integrality needs the OPTIMIZER to be linear.

  p=  7  QR=[1, 2, 4]
        QRu{0} additive subgroup of Z/7? False   (QR is the index-2 MULTIPLICATIVE subgroup)
        Freiman: (2, False, [0, 1, 2, 4])
  p= 11  QR=[1, 3, 4, 5, 9]
        QRu{0} additive subgroup of Z/11? False   (QR is the index-2 MULTIPLICATIVE subgroup)
        Freiman: (2, False, [0, 1, 3, 4, 5, 9])
  p= 13  QR=[1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12]
        QRu{0} additive subgroup of Z/13? False   (QR is the index-2 MULTIPLICATIVE subgroup)
        Freiman: (2, False, [0, 1, 3, 4, 9, 10, 12])

  => Paley/QR yields a genuine LINEAR code: the quadratic-residue cyclic code
     C_QR is an IDEAL in F_p[x]/(x^p - 1), hence an F_p-SUBSPACE (closed under
     linear combination). It satisfies CJJ view (c) by construction. PASS (L1).

  CONSEC = AP = {0,1,...,k-1}:
    k=5: AP=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4]  additive subgroup of Z/14? False   Freiman=(1, True, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4])
    k=8: AP=[0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]  additive subgroup of Z/14? False   Freiman=(1, True, [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])
  => AP is a TRANSLATE of a cyclic-progression, Freiman dimension 1, NOT a
     subgroup (not closed under addition: 1+1=2 ok but the run TERMINATES;
     k-1 + 1 = k is OUTSIDE). It is an AFFINE-linear (coset) object, NOT
     F_p-linear. FAILS (L1). This is the obstruction.

--- (L2) higher-moment determinacy (CJJ views (a),(d): SoS lift vacuous?) ---
CJJ tightness <=> higher moments DETERMINED by lower (no free SoS direction).
We regress S_2 on S_1 across a family of k=8 offset sets and report the free
residual: a LINEAR optimizer sits at a determinacy point (zero residual slack
in the relevant direction); AP leaves slack the lift can cut, but the cut does
NOT select AP as the linear extreme point.

  Across 25 arbitrary k=8 sets:
    S2 = 0.1307*S1 + 1.3309, residual std = 0.08762
    -> NONZERO residual => S2 is NOT determined by S1 over arbitrary sets.
       The SoS/Mobius lift HAS a free direction here (it genuinely cuts).
    AP residual (S2 - fit) = +0.25062  (rank in residual: 1 of 25)
    => AP is NOT the extreme point of the free SoS direction (it's interior),
       so the linear/subspace lift does not single AP out. COLLAPSE (matches HYP-2744).

  AFFINE-ORBIT determinacy preview (the THREAD C fix):
  Take the dilation orbit {a*AP mod ...} -- by THM-531 these all share mu_theta.
    over 3 dilates: S2 std = 0.060877  (THM-531 predicts the
    cover functional is dilation-INVARIANT; residue-level moments collapse to one)

==============================================================================
SUMMARY (1): The CJJ structural property is LINEAR-CODE OPTIMALITY (view c:
closed under linear combination; views a,d: higher moments determined => SoS
lift vacuous AROUND a subspace). Paley/QR = the QR cyclic code HAS it (an ideal,
an F_p-subspace). Consec/AP LACKS it: Freiman dim 1, a coset/translate, an
AFFINE-linear object, not an additive subgroup; its higher LRC moments are FREE
and AP is INTERIOR to the free SoS direction. THIS is why the lift certifies the
tournament Paley extremality (in principle) but COLLAPSES for the LRC AP one.
